This directory is where your work goes.

Inside the container it appears at ~/projects. It is the ONLY directory shared between
the container and your own computer, which means two things worth knowing:

  * Anything you keep here is safe. `cs193v --rebuild` and `cs193v --full-rebuild` never
    touch it, because it lives on your computer rather than inside the container.

  * Anything you keep here is visible to the container, and therefore to any code the
    agent runs. Treat API keys accordingly, and prefer throwaway ones for coursework.

Make a directory per project. There is no structure to conform to.

This file exists only so the directory is present before the container starts.
